@Main Menu@40/20/560/170
\C3\s\s\s\s\s\s\s\s\s\s---------- Main Menu ----------\n\n
\C2Read Mail\C1 -  Open a mail packet and read messages.\n\n
\C2Config AmiQWK\C1 - AmiQWK Configuration Editor.\n\n
\C2About AmiQWK\C1 - Display info about program.\n\n
\C2Quit AmiQWK\C1 - Exit program.\n\n\n
You may use the keys \C2R,C,A, and Q\C1 in place of the gadgets.\n\n
Press the \C2Help\C1 or \C2F1\C1 key at any time for context sensitive help.
\@
@Configuration Editor@40/20/560/170
\C3\s\s\s\s\s\s\s\s\s\s---------- Configuration Editor. ----------\n\n
\C2Message Text Font\C1 - Font (8 point monospaced) used to display message text.
Topaz 8 used if no font is specified.\n\n
\C2Reply Quote Prefix\C1 - Short prefix added to each line of message text that
is quoted in a reply to set appart your text from the message text you are
quoting from.\n\n
\C2Edit Palette\C1 - Change the color values for the AmiQWK custom screen.\n\n
\C2Edit Compression Command Strings\C1 - Edit the command line strings used for
packing replies.\n\n
\C2Edit Decompression Command Strings\C1 - Edit the command line strings for
extracting mail packets.\n\n
\C2Editor\C1 - name (and path, if needed) of the text editor you wish to use.\n\n
\C2Work Directory\C1 - Directory where AmiQWK will extract mail packets to.\n
\C3\s\s\s\s\s\s\s\s\s\sTHIS SHOULD NOT BE AN EXISTING DIRECTORY!\n
\C3\s\s\s\s\s\s\s\s\s\sALL FILES IN THIS DIRECTORY WILL BE DELETED.\n
\C3\s\s\s\s\s\s\s\s\s\sAmiQWK WILL CREATE THIS DIRECTORY AUTOMATICALY.\n\n
\C2Packet Directory\C1 - Directory where AmiQWK will look for mail packets. Set
this to the downloads directory your term program uses.\n\n
\C2Reply Directory\C1 - Directory where AmiQWK will put replies. Set this to the
uploads directory your term program uses.\n\n
\C2Cancel\C1 - Discard changes to configuration and return to main menu.\n\n
\C2Save\C1 - Save new configuration to disk.\n\n
\C2OK\C1 - Use new configuration.
\@
@Read Messages@40/20/560/170
\C3\s\s\s\s\s\s\s\s\s\s---------- Read Messages ----------\n\n
\C1 The following keys can be used when reading messages.\n\n
\C2Left Arrow, Numeric Keypad 4\C1 - Read Previous message.\n\n
\C2Right Arrow, Numeric Keypad 6\C1 - Read Next message.\n\n
\C2Up Arrow, Numeric Keypad 8\C1 - Scroll message up 1 line.\n\n
\C2Down Arrow, Numeric Keypad 2\C1 - Scroll message down 1 line.\n\n
\C2Numeric Keypad 1\C1 - Jump to End of message.\n\n
\C2Numeric Keypad 3\C1 - Scroll message down 1 page.\n\n
\C2Numeric Keypad 7\C1 - Jump to Begining of message.\n\n
\C2Numeric Keypad 9\C1 - Scroll message up 1 page.\n\n
\C2C\C1 - Select new Conference.\n\n
\C2Q\C1 - Quit to Main Menu.\n\n
\C2R\C1 - Reply to message.\n\n
\C2E\C1 - Enter a new message.
\@
@Reply/New Message@40/20/560/170
\C3\s\s\s\s\s\s\s\s\s\s---------- Reply/New Message ----------\n\n
\C2From\C1 - Person message is from (Usually your own name, unless
possibly the message is posted onto a conference where aliases are
allowed.\n\n
\C2To\C1 - Person you are sending the messgae to.\n\n
\C2Subject\C1 - Subject of the message.\n\n
\C2Conference\C1 - Select Conference. Click on the 'Conference' gadget to
bring up a conference requester, or type the conference number into the
intiger gadget. The conference name will be displayed in the box to the
right.\n\n
\C2Public/Private\C1 - Select public or private status of message. If
gadget is selected (Hilighted and recessed) the message will be private.\n\n
\C2Select Tagline\C1 - Not Implimented Yet. A future version of AmiQWK will
have the capibility to store a collection of taglines and allow you to
select between them.\n\n
\C2Tagline\C1 - Tagline to be added to this message. Until the above
'Select Tagline' feature is implimented, this will display a default
tagline. You can change this to anything up to 60 characters.\n\n
\C2Cancel\C1 - Cancel Reply/New Message. Do not add a new message.\n\n
\C2OK\C1 - Enter Message. AmiQWK will start the text editor you selected in
the configuration editor. if you are replying to a message the old message
will be quoted using the quote string you specified in the configuration
editor. When you have finished editing your reply, the Reply/New Message
requester will be displayed agian. You can change any of the fields in the
requester, (to, from, subject, ect.) or if you decided that you do not want
to send the message, you can click on the 'Cancel' gadget. Otherwise click
on the 'OK' gadget and your reply will be added to the list of replies.
\@